      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "Dwarven tunnels and mines"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A small smooth-coated tunnel dog with a long body, triangular ears, strong short legs, and oversized front paws."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Senses",
          "lines": [
            "Blindsense 40 ft."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Traits mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Heightened Hearing · Perception is 17 for hearing."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Actions mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Bite · +5 to hit · reach 5 ft. · One target takes 5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage on a hit. · 1d4 + 3 piercing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Reactions mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Reflexive Escape · When attacked by a creature it can see, the kamrat can move up to 5 ft. The attack misses if that puts it out of reach."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Variant options mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Variant selection · Choose at most one option. It replaces Reflexive Escape.",
            "Dedicated Target (bonus action) · Choose one creature the kamrat can see. It has advantage on attacks against that creature and on ability checks to track or follow it while it can see the target and for 3 hours after losing sight of it.",
            "Frenetic (bonus action) · The kamrat takes the Disengage or Hide action.",
            "Digger (trait) · This variant has a 5-ft. burrowing speed."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "Printed Perception 12, Stealth 15. Ability modifiers are Str −1, Dex +5, Con +2, Int −4, Wis +2, Cha −1.",
            "The ordinary kamrat has only the printed 30-ft. walking speed. The source classifies its echo sensing as blindsense."
          ]
        }
      ],
